traight to the earth  and that would be a huge problem but  what also proved to be a problem is that  you're not allowed to intersect the  scenery with the coaster track so none  of the supports actually touch the  coaster I try to get as close as I could  with making all of these custom supports  and get them to almost intersect the  coaster track but at no point do the  supports even touch the track there is  always a super super small distance  between the supports and the track so  it's not actually technically supported  I just needed to get all of these  supports and to create the illusion of  everything being pulled toward the  planets which I have here these supports  are also the reason why the track isn't  really longer than it is since custom  supporting on its own is already quite  challenging with you know not being able  to put the supports into the coaster  track but with these supports I also had  to make sure that every support goes  directly into the center of the planets  so it took a lot of trial and error to  get all of these supports to go into the  right direction and actually supports  the coaster in a way that would make  sense if this  it actually had a gravitational pull so  um yeah in the end that meant making a  lot of these different supports and I  cut out a lot of the support making from  the time-lapse videos I think it's just  a bit of a boring thing it's something I  had to do but nothing that really  defines the coaster the only case in  which I would say I think these supports  are very defining in this sort of  scenery kind of purpose it is for the  tallest points the first 0 0 has some  supports that always take out from the  planets and you can see very clearly and  the same goes for this original the  zero-g roll that launches over the  station which has some tall supports  which kind of fit a scenery kind of  purpose they just make it seem even more  like it's a small planet and it's a  small planet with actual gravity but  